        "raw_html_sha256": "86fd75bdd7d147c31ac8891f810bf4abab23c368772495078e77cbdd39736fca",
        "text": "Zones contain a lower, main section, used for resizing and moving the zone itself, and a narrow upper section that defines fade ranges. Resizing of either section is done by clicking and dragging on its right or left edges, while moving is accomplished by clicking and dragging a zone from anywhere except its edges."
      },
      "reason": "B044 assigns the lower main section the role of resizing/moving the zone itself, then explicitly permits resizing either section from its edges and describes moving a zone from anywhere except its edges. The new grouped grammar says both main and fade sections move, which can impose an independent fade-range interior-translation gesture not separately established by this prose. This is a source-role/gesture-target clarification, not a claim that such a gesture cannot exist in Live or that the source contradicts itself. Null numerical/actual oracles do not make the normative role expansion harmless.",
      "minimal_correction": "In a preserved successor split the two roles: resize main and fade sections from their respective left/right edges; move the zone itself by an admitted interior drag, conservatively the lower main section. Make RCK066 actual action name the whole zone as the move target. Any independent fade-section translation remains U unless separately supported. Preserve all R2 bytes, IDs/counts, source_claims/pointers/oracles/guards and old61records, and add a focused rejection fixture for the conflation.",
